if you're struggling to decide whether  you should stay in school go get a job  or start your own business I'm gonna  help answer that question for you today  on this video hi I'm Evan Carmichael  I believe in entrepreneurs and I  recently got a question from one of my  subscribers love you guys  Paul who wrote in the say hi I'm Paul  right now I have faced some problems  that myself couldn't solve can you  please help me solve it my problem is  that I'm very unclear and vague at the  future I do not know if I should focus  myself on school now to try getting into  Stanford or go get a job  lease an office and work with my  classmates I'm obsessed with starting  the business but did not know how to  take the first step right can you please  help me give me a clear path of which  direction I should really take please  help me with this step thank you  commit Paul Paul is a fantastic question  and one I want you to know you're not  alone everybody goes through this  multiple times in their life you are not  the only one in the world going through  this right now with all big decisions my  advice always is to follow your heart  and not your head follow what feels  right  follow your passion even if it doesn't  make any sense at all because that's  gonna be the path that will lead you to  success and a happier life see a lot of  people tell you to do the safe thing do  the smart thing most people will go to  school and then get a job and then stay  in that career forever and ever and ever  and they end up hating their life as  years go on you start hating what you're  doing more and more and more and you're  living for the evenings and weekends and  the scary thing is that's most people  that is most people in the world most  people are not living their dreams  because they did the safe thing and they  listened to their head the logical thing  to do instead of the heart which was the  passionate thing to do and the scary  thing is quite often the people that you  take advice from the people who are  asking help from are those very same  people who were too afraid to ever risk  anything and bet on themselves they took  that safe path and so what's their  advice gonna be to take the same path  for you as well where if you look at the  top people in any field on  burners artists exactly if you look at  the top people in any field then people  were at the top of the top their passion  about what they did they are passionate  about continually about what they're  doing and they're exploring new things  even if it doesn't make any logical  sense because they're listening to their  heart and not their head so I can't tell  you what to do I can't tell you go to  Stanford I can't tell you start a job I  can't tell you go and start this  entrepreneurial venture from your email  from the question it sounds like when  you said I'm obsessed with starting the  business you want to follow that  obsession right that's where I'm  thinking you should be but it's gotta be  coming from your heart if you love  Stanford nuts bring your dream that's  where you want to go to go to Stanford  not everybody is supposed to be an  entrepreneur but if you love being an  entrepreneur that's what you want to  learn about even if there's nobody in  your families but an entrepreneur even  if you have no resources or connections  or ideas yet you will learn when you are  excited about something that's when you  really learn and pick it up and I don't  want you to live in regret I don't want  you to look back on your life when  you're 70 80 90 years old and you did  the same thing and you say to yourself I  really wish when I was 20 years old or  however old you are that I bet on myself  I really wish that I had taken that  chance because now you've lived that  entire life and you always are gonna be  wondering what if I want to share a bit  of a personal story to help bring this  home my sister works for the United  Nations and she had an opportunity to go  to a really dangerous part of the world  and my parents were telling me hey Evan  you know she listens to you tell her not  to go this is really silly it's stupid  she could get killed it's really  dangerous there if she shouldn't go and  I get that as parents you know myself  being a father you are always worried  about your children and as a brother  I want my sister to be safe you know I  want her to do things where she doesn't  have a risk of dying right I don't face  that risk in my profession but she  doesn't hers and when she asked me for  advice  I had to shut off all my brotherly  instincts I had to shut off the desire  for her to be safe to desire for her to  you know not get killed the desire for  me to want to see her every Christmas  because I don't want her to have to live  in regret I don't want her to live the  rest of her life wondering what F and so  I told her the same thing that I'm  telling you guys big decisions you make  with the heart and not the head I told  her to trust her gut I told her to  follow her passion and do what she felt  was right now she ended up not taking  that job and I'm so so so so relieved  but she did it for her she did it for  the right reasons not because other  people told her to do it  and so that's the key whether you're  thinking about school job starting the  business or any other big decision in  your life always listen to your heart  not your head and don't listen to other  people who are too afraid to chase their  dreams and take their advice and live  their version of your life instead of  your version of your own life believe so  those are you watching I'd love to hear  your thoughts on how you decided to  start your business or how you decided  to go from taking on a school or taking  on a job or taking on a company leave it  in the comments below I'm looking  forward to getting involved in that  discussion and if you liked this video  and you want to see more don't forget to  subscribe to the channel and the  newsletter thank you so much for  watching I'll see you soon

